Subject: [Rpy] New RPy Release: 1.0RC3
Message-ID: <391D6002-8116-4E83-B67A-25982F3F0FC4@rochester.edu>

Hello Everyone,

RPy version 1.0RC3 is now available.  This release fixes a major bug  
with recent versions of R on non-Windows systems and adds support for  
NumPy.

Enjoy!

-Greg

===============


CHANGES in RPY 1.0RC3 - 2007-06-26
----------------------------------

New Features:

   - Now supports NumPy in addtion to Numeric, thanks to work by
     Alexander Belopolsky


Bug Fixes:

   - Applied patch created by Andrew McNamara that resolves the C stack
     limit error produced by R in some contexts, such as resizing the
     x11() window.


CHANGES in RPY 1.0RC2 - 2006-12-11
----------------------------------

New Features:

   - Add support for newer versions of R

Bug Fixes:

   - Made changes to avoid need for R/bin in PATH


CHANGES in RPY 1.0RC1 - 2006-08-08
----------------------------------

Bug Fixes:


   - Modify version string parsing to handle format changes related  
to R 2.3.0
     and later

   - Enhancements to documentation generation  (submitted by Dirk
     Eddelbuettel)

